  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Navigate to Avatars from Quick Menu\n\n3. Navigate to Shop (avatars shop)\n\n4. Check the \"New\" category (\"View All\")\n\n5. Try to click on a few avatars until you find unobtainable avatar products with avatar visibility set to Private (?).\n\nAffected avatars/products:\n\n- Eldritch Low Poly Plushies˸ Mouse Opossum Ver (`avtr_0c344df6-2b19-4d6b-9276-baee5938bebf`) by EldritchElias (`prod_bfe7407d-40b2-407c-bc6f-53a04aa39e1e`)\n\n- Eldritch Low Poly Plushies˸ Water Opossum Ver (`avtr_4550a6c5-a131-4fda-affe-d6aef1e9dff0`) by EldritchElias (`prod_6d4af10f-9400-41d7-82cb-d998506e7145`)\n\nThis is reproducible consistently with affected products and persists with client restarts.\n\nUsing the [Private Avatar Information Leak](https://feedback.vrchat.com/website/p/private-avatar-information-leak) bug to view the metadata of these avatars via HTML meta tags, the avatars seem to exist under said ID, but may be set to Private status / require a purchase.\n\nExpected behavior: \"That listing doesn't exist․ It may have been removed․\" message or similar indicating temporary (or permanent) product listing unavailability. Alternatively, not listed in the shop at all.\n\nActual behavior: Listed in the Shop with a name and thumbnail, but \"Avatar Not Found\" once clicked. (not accurate) Clicking on an avatar changes the listing to \"Unavailable\". The \"That listing doesn't exist․ It may have been removed․\" response from API is not displayed in the client for the product listing.",
